  "description": "New York's 7th Congressional District, covering parts of western Queens and north Brooklyn (including Long Island City, Greenpoint, and Williamsburg), is holding an open-seat election following the retirement of 16-term Democratic incumbent Nydia Vel\u00e1zquez. The Democratic primary, scheduled for June 23, 2026, is a competitive four-way contest between Brooklyn Borough President Antonio Reynoso, Assembly Member Claire Valdez, City Council Member Julie Won, and public defender Vichal Kumar. The winner will be heavily favored in the general election in this solidly Democratic district, which has long been a progressive stronghold. The Republican candidate, community activist Melvin Rivera, advanced unopposed from the Republican primary.",
